Package: BARCS
Type: Package
Title: Beta-Binomial Analysis and Regression for CRISPR Pooled Screens
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
  c(person(given = "Hyun-Hwan", family = "Jeong", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "hyun-hwan.jeong@bcm.edu"))
Description: Fits guide-level beta-binomial regression to pooled CRISPR screen
  counts on an arbitrary full-rank design matrix, and tests a prespecified
  coefficient or linear contrast against a Student t reference whose degrees of
  freedom come from independent sequenced libraries rather than read depth.
  Guide counts are modeled against unfiltered full-library totals, so a
  beta-binomial variance separates sequencing precision from between-library
  heterogeneity. Optional negative-control calibration and guide-dispersion
  moderation are provided, together with several guide-to-gene summaries.
  The two-group special case and its method are described in Jeong et al.
  (2019) <doi:10.1101/gr.245571.118>; the overdispersed regression construction
  follows Baggerly et al. (2004) <doi:10.1186/1471-2105-5-144>.
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)
